<BaseLayout title="Body Areas – Acupressure Points by Region" description="Browse acupressure points organized by body region. Explore detailed guides for points on the head, face, hands, feet, back, and limbs with location maps and benefits." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Body Atlas", href: "/atlas" }, { label: "Body Regions", href: "/body" }]} datePublished="2025-04-01" dateModified="2026-05-15" articleSchema={true}>
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6"><div class="mb-8 rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 p-5 dark:border-emerald-900/50 dark:bg-emerald-900/20"><p class="text-sm text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 leading-relaxed"><strong>Not sure where to start?</strong> Use the <a href="/tools/pain-map" class="font-medium underline decoration-emerald-400 underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-700 dark:hover:text-emerald-100">interactive pain map</a> — tap the body region that hurts to see the most common causes, the red-flag symptoms that need a doctor, and the best points and condition guides for that area.</p></div><div class="text-center mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">Acupressure Points by Body Region</h1><p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">Explore acupressure points organized by body region. Each guide covers the key points in that area — their exact locations, clinical benefits, proper stimulation techniques, and related conditions they can help manage. Click a region below to discover its pressure points.</p></div><div class="mb-10"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">How Points Are Organized by Region</h2><p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">The body's acupressure points are grouped into twelve regions that follow natural anatomy: head, face, ears, neck, shoulders, hands, arms and wrists, chest, abdomen, back, legs, and feet. Each region guide lists the key points in that area, their exact locations, traditional uses, and how to stimulate them. Browsing by region is the fastest way to find points when you know where you feel the problem but not the point name.</p><p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">Two regions are especially good for beginners. The hand guide covers LI4 (Hegu), HT7 (Shenmen), and other points that are quick, visible, and easy to reach for headaches, nausea, and stress. The foot guide includes KI1 (Yongquan), LV3 (Taichong), and points behind the ankle that many people find grounding and simple to press barefoot.</p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">Regions, Meridians, and Conditions</h2><p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">Regions and condition guides work together. In TCM, points along a meridian connect distant parts of the body — a headache routine commonly combines head points such as GB20 (Fengchi) with the hand point LI4 (Hegu), while sleep and anxiety guides pair wrist and face points such as HT7 and Yintang. Back pain routines draw on points along the Bladder meridian, which runs down the back and legs, including BL40 (Weizhong) and BL60 (Kunlun). If a condition guide mentions a point that is hard to reach, the region pages will show nearby alternatives.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4"><a href="/body/head-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">H</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Head</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Scalp and forehead points for headaches, stress, and mental clarity</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/face-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">F</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Face</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Facial and auricular points for relaxation and sinus health</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/ear-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">E</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Ear</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Auricular therapy points for whole-body wellness</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/neck-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">N</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Neck</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Points for neck tension, headache prevention, and mobility</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/shoulder-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">S</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Shoulder</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Relieve shoulder tension and improve range of motion</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/hand-acupressure-chart" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">H</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Hand</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">All major hand and wrist points for quick relief</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/arm-wrist-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">A</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Arm &amp; Wrist</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">LI4, PC6, and other key arm points for pain and nausea</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/chest-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">C</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Chest</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Points for respiratory health, anxiety, and heart calming</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/abdomen-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">A</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Abdomen</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Digestive health and core vitality points</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/back-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">B</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Back</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Organ health and back pain relief through shu points</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/leg-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">L</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Leg</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">ST36, SP6, and other major leg points for energy and health</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a><a href="/body/foot-acupressure-points" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 transition-all hover:border-emerald-400 hover:shadow-sm dark:border-stone-700 dark:bg-stone-900 dark:hover:border-emerald-600"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-sm font-bold mb-3">F</div><h2 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Foot</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Guide to foot points for grounding and wellness</p><span class="mt-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">Browse Points →</span></a></div><div class="mt-10"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900 mb-3"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Which region should I start with?</summary><div class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">The hand and foot regions are the easiest starting points: their points are simple to find, easy to reach, and cover common needs such as headaches, nausea, stress, and sleep. From there, move to the region that matches your symptoms.</div></details><details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900 mb-3"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Why do different regions treat the same problem?</summary><div class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">Meridians connect distant regions, so several points can target one condition. Headaches, for example, are often treated with GB20 at the base of the skull together with LI4 on the hand. Combining regions is normal and often more comfortable than pressing one spot for long.</div></details><details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900 mb-3"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Can I reach back points myself?</summary><div class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">Some back points are easy to reach, but others such as BL23 (Shenshu) and BL40 (Weizhong) are awkward on your own. A massage stick, a tennis ball pressed against a wall, or a partner can apply steady pressure there.</div></details><details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Are some regions better than others?</summary><div class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">No single region is best — the right choice depends on your symptom and how easily you can reach the point. Beginners often prefer the hand and foot, while someone with neck tension may get more from the neck and shoulder guides.</div></details></div></div>
</BaseLayout>